# ===== Symfony Task Manager Web App =====

1. Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/beltranmelifliba-sketch/Task-manager.git
cd task-manager

2. Install PHP Dependencies

Sa loob ng project folder, i-run:

composer install

3. Configure Environment

Kung may .env.example file:

copy .env.example .env

I-update ang database credentials sa .env file kung kinakailangan.

Example:

DATABASE_URL="mysql://root:@127.0.0.1:3306/task_manager"

4. Create the Database

CREATE DATABASE task_manager;

O gamit ang Symfony:

php bin/console doctrine:database:create

5. Run Database Migrations

php bin/console doctrine:migrations:migrate

Type:

yes

kapag may confirmation prompt.

Run the Application
Option A: Using Symfony CLI
Verify Symfony CLI Installation
symfony -v

Dapat may lumabas na Symfony CLI version.

Start the Development Server
symfony server:start

Open in Browser
http://127.0.0.1:8000/task

Stop the Server
symfony server:stop

Option B: Using PHP Built-in Server

Kung walang Symfony CLI:

php -S 127.0.0.1:8000 -t public

Pagkatapos buksan:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/task
Troubleshooting
Missing Vendor Files

Run:

composer install
Clear Symfony Cache
php bin/console cache:clear
Verify Routes
php bin/console debug:router


